# `include_str!` embeds a file's bytes verbatim. On Windows,
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the default from Git for Windows' installer and
# converts every LF in a tracked text file to CRLF on checkout -- after which
# the embedded copy differs from the LF text the generator produces on every
# single line, for a reason that has nothing to do with the port. `-text`
# disables that conversion in both directions.
#
# Not theoretical: this is what failed the first v2.2.1 release build, on
# `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` -- the one Windows target whose runner executes the
# tests it builds.
#
# Note the asymmetry: `src/**.rs` needs no such rule. `GENERATED_DEFAULT_CONFIG`
# is a raw string literal, and rustc normalises CRLF to LF inside string
# literals, so the constant survives a converted checkout where the file it is
# compared against does not.
src/testdata/**   -text
